<title>FRANCE: French dairy farmers protest falling prices.</title>
<headline>French dairy farmers protest falling prices.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dairy farmers blocked deliveries to hypermarkets in various parts of France on Tuesday in a protest against falling milk prices, unions said.</p>
<p>The protesters set up roadblocks before dawn and turned back delivery trucks, accusing big distribution firms of gradually pushing down milk prices.</p>
<p>&quot;We cannot accept a downwards price spiral until year 2000, because we would never regain what we would have lost,&quot; a union spokesman said. He called for the government to set up a crisis unit to discuss farmers' grievances.</p>
<p>Asked about the protest, Prime Minister Alain Juppe told RTL radio it could be settled by talks. &quot;Conflicts are solved through talks...We have solved many of them,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
